## Regression: an instance method that takes a closure/any-Fn parameter
## AND returns a heap value (Array) must round-trip the return value across
## the call boundary intact.
##
## Root cause (fixed): method selection counted only positional args and
## ignored a trailing `do…end` block satisfying the method's closure
## parameter, so the call's return type degraded to a fresh inference var
## (`Infer`) instead of `Array[Int]`. With the return un-typed as an Array,
## the MIR index lowering bailed and `arr[0]` read a stale buffer pointer.
class Box
  v: Int
  def init(v: Int)
    self.v = v
  end
  def probe(f: any Fn[Fn(Int) -> Int]) -> Array[Int]
    var out: Array[Int] = Array.new
    out.push(f.(3))
    out
  end
end

def main
  let b = Box.new(0)
  let arr = b.probe do |x| x + 100 end
  puts "#{arr[0]}"
end
